Subject: [PATCH] [mlir][dataflow] Keep a state's maps and sets inline when small

Every lattice anchor with a state has an inner
`DenseMap<TypeID, std::unique_ptr<AnalysisState>>`, and every state
with a dependent a `SetVector<WorkItem>`. LLVM's `DenseMap` never
allocates fewer than 64 buckets once it holds anything, and a
`SetVector` with no inline size starts a 64-bucket `DenseSet` at its
first insert, so "this value has a state" costs two minimum-size hash
tables, about 2.9 KB for one bit of liveness measured on arm64 macOS,
more than 90 percent of it the two tables.

An anchor holds the states of one or two analyses, so its map is now a
`SmallDenseMap<TypeID, ..., 2>`, and a state's dependents a `SetVector`
with 4 inline elements: about 0.2 KB per state, fifteenfold less, with
no API change. The solver runs on one thread, so its program-point
uniquer no longer takes locks (`disableMultithreading`).
---
diff --git a/mlir/include/mlir/Analysis/DataFlowFramework.h b/mlir/include/mlir/Analysis/DataFlowFramework.h
index b9dc9609..9609053f 100644
--- a/mlir/include/mlir/Analysis/DataFlowFramework.h
+++ b/mlir/include/mlir/Analysis/DataFlowFramework.h
@@ -329,6 +329,8 @@ public:
   explicit DataFlowSolver(const DataFlowConfig &config = DataFlowConfig())
       : config(config) {
     uniquer.registerParametricStorageType<ProgramPoint>();
+    // The solver runs on one thread, so its program points need no locks.
+    uniquer.disableMultithreading();
   }
 
   /// Load an analysis into the solver. Return the analysis instance.
@@ -485,8 +487,11 @@ private:
   StorageUniquer uniquer;
 
   /// A type-erased map of lattice anchors to associated analysis states for
-  /// first-class lattice anchors.
-  DenseMap<LatticeAnchor, DenseMap<TypeID, std::unique_ptr<AnalysisState>>>
+  /// first-class lattice anchors. An anchor holds the states of one or two
+  /// analyses, so its map stays inline: a `DenseMap` allocates 64 buckets
+  /// once it holds anything, about 1 KiB per anchor.
+  DenseMap<LatticeAnchor,
+           SmallDenseMap<TypeID, std::unique_ptr<AnalysisState>, 2>>
       analysisStates;
 
   /// A map of Ananlysis state type to the equivalent lattice anchors.
@@ -563,8 +568,12 @@ private:
   /// pushed to the back of the queue. Use a `SetVector` to keep the analysis
   /// deterministic.
   ///
-  /// Store the dependents on the analysis state for efficiency.
-  SetVector<DataFlowSolver::WorkItem> dependents;
+  /// Store the dependents on the analysis state for efficiency. A state has a
+  /// few dependents, so the set stays inline until it grows: a `SetVector`
+  /// with no inline size starts a 64-bucket `DenseSet` at its first insert.
+  SetVector<DataFlowSolver::WorkItem, SmallVector<DataFlowSolver::WorkItem, 0>,
+            DenseSet<DataFlowSolver::WorkItem>, 4>
+      dependents;
 
   /// Allow the framework to access the dependents.
   friend class DataFlowSolver;
